// The sheet's own duration is Concentration(60) ("a blade ... you swing at
// foes within reach ... until your focus fades"), but there is no
// persistent-conjured-weapon-summon mechanism anywhere in this engine that
// would need a real 60 s timer -- this ships as an ordinary repeatable
// player-triggered melee strike, mechanically identical to any other
// BasicMelee spell (see booming_blade.ron/green_flame_blade.ron, Wave 1,
// which are cast on demand with no timer either). The compendium entry
// below lists duration: Instant rather than Concentration(60) for the same
// reason divine_favor.ron (Wave 1) does: a 60 s "active" claim in the
// in-game spellbook tooltip would promise a persistence this ability
// doesn't have.
//
// Sear is used over Stab/Slash/Bash/Hook for its built-in Burning rider
// (common/src/comp/melee.rs), the closest fire-flavored kind available (see
// booming_blade.ron for why no MeleeConstructorKind exposes a real Fire
// damage_kind field -- Sear's own hardcoded kind is Energy, not Fire).
BasicMelee(
    energy_cost: 20,
    buildup_duration: 0.4,
    swing_duration: 0.1,
    hit_timing: 0.5,
    recover_duration: 0.3,
    melee_constructor: (
        kind: Sear(damage: 22, poise: 8, knockback: 0, energy_regen: 0),
        range: 3.0,
        angle: 20.0,
    ),
    meta: (school: Some(Evocation), source: Some(Arcane)),
)
